{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Keep the five-year ILR route for UK-educated Skilled Workers",
        "additional_details": "UK-educated graduates pay high tuition, Graduate (PSW) visa fees, repeated Immigration Health Surcharges and Skilled Worker costs, then Income Tax and National Insurance. Extending ILR to ten years risks treating them as cash cows, forced to pay immigration charges longer despite lawful contributions. Many work for northern start-ups and engineering firms where \u00a350,271 salaries are unrealistic. This could deter students, harm investment and recruitment, and punish those who followed the rules.",
        "background": "Keep the five-year ILR pathway for UK-educated graduates who progress from Student or Graduate (PSW) visas into sponsored skilled work, meet immigration rules and pay taxes. Do not impose the \u00a350,271 earnings threshold on this group, and protect existing Skilled Workers from the ten-year change.",
